---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import Eyebrow from "../../components/Eyebrow.astro";
---
<SiteLayout
  title="Cisco Networking — fred.fish"
  description="A practical Cisco networking workspace with a structured CCNA curriculum, adaptive practice, and organized IOS XE references."
  active="cisco"
>
  <section class="page-intro cisco-intro">
    <Eyebrow index="01" label="NETWORKING WORKSPACE / CISCO" />
    <h1>Understand the network.<br /><span>Configure with confidence.</span></h1>
    <p>A growing technical workspace for learning networking, practising configurations, and keeping useful Cisco IOS XE references close at hand.</p>
    <div class="intro-actions">
      <a class="button button-primary" href="/cisco/learning/">Explore the curriculum <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <a class="button" href="/cisco/practice/">Start adaptive practice <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cisco-overview" aria-label="Cisco workspace sections">
    <a class="cisco-card cisco-card-feature" href="/cisco/learning/">
      <div class="cisco-card-top"><span class="cisco-card-icon" aria-hidden="true">⌘</span><span class="cisco-card-label">01 / LEARN</span><span class="cisco-card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      <div><h2>Networking curriculum</h2><p>Build a strong foundation from physical-layer concepts through switching, routing, services, security, and automation.</p></div>
      <div class="cisco-card-metrics"><span><strong>30</strong> modules</span><span>CCNA 200-301 aligned</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="cisco-card" href="/cisco/practice/">
      <div class="cisco-card-top"><span class="cisco-card-icon" aria-hidden="true">◎</span><span class="cisco-card-label">02 / PRACTICE</span><span class="cisco-card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      <div><h2>Adaptive practice</h2><p>Short quiz sessions that track individual concepts, reinforce weak areas, and revisit mastered topics over time.</p></div>
      <span class="cisco-card-cta">Start a 10-question session <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span>
    </a>
    <a class="cisco-card" href="/cisco/progress/">
      <div class="cisco-card-top"><span class="cisco-card-icon" aria-hidden="true">▥</span><span class="cisco-card-label">03 / PROGRESS</span><span class="cisco-card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      <div><h2>Learning dashboard</h2><p>See concept mastery, accuracy, session history, and the concepts that need your attention next.</p></div>
      <span class="cisco-card-cta">Review progress <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span>
    </a>
    <a class="cisco-card" href="/cisco/reference/">
      <div class="cisco-card-top"><span class="cisco-card-icon" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span><span class="cisco-card-label">04 / REFERENCE</span><span class="cisco-card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      <div><h2>IOS XE reference</h2><p>Keep commands, configuration patterns, verification steps, and troubleshooting notes organized in one place.</p></div>
      <span class="cisco-card-cta">Browse references <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span>
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="cisco-note">
    <Eyebrow label="HOW THIS WORKSPACE IS ORGANIZED" />
    <h2>Learn it. Build it. Verify it.</h2>
    <p>Use the lessons to understand the underlying protocols, then return to the reference material when configuring or troubleshooting devices. The curriculum and command reference are designed to work together.</p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
